---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAEcCwzuExy2fSCmH';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Strategic Direction | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="For teams with a strategic opportunity but fuzzy direction. Saielle helps you find the right problem before you build the wrong thing."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Leadership &amp; advisory</p>
      <h1>Find the right problem before you build the wrong thing.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For teams with a strategic opportunity but fuzzy direction.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Everyone has a different opinion about what you should do. The board
        wants progress. The technology is moving faster than the organisation.
        Nobody really owns the whole problem.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most transformations fail here, before a line of code is written.
        Not because the team lacks talent, but because nobody has a shared
        answer to a basic question: what are we actually trying to do?
      </p>

      <h2>Sound familiar?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Three teams, three strategies, no shared answer to "what are we building and why?"</li>
        <li>The board wants a roadmap. You do not have a thesis.</li>
        <li>Technology is moving faster than the organisation can decide.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I come in for a fixed period to establish clarity. Not a roadmap
        deck. A shared understanding of the problem, the strategic thesis,
        the product direction and the measures that tell you whether you are
        making progress.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work with your leadership team to surface assumptions, test the
        strategic thesis and make the implicit explicit.
      </p>

      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The problem or opportunity, clearly framed</li>
        <li>A strategic thesis the leadership team actually believes</li>
        <li>Product direction and prioritisation logic</li>
        <li>An operating model that matches the work</li>
        <li>Measures of success you can track, not just report</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Typically two to four weeks. Two or three days a week. Enough time
        to listen, diagnose and synthesize, not so long that urgency
        dissipates.
      </p>
      <p>
        The engagement ends with a direction document and a set of decisions
        your team can act on immediately.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
        <p class="form-lede">
          If your team is stuck between a big opportunity and a fuzzy plan,
          that is exactly the work I do.
        </p>
        <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="source" value="strategic-direction" />
          <div class="form-grid">
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Name</span>
              <input type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Email</span>
              <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </label>
          </div>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">What's this about?</span>
            <select name="topic">
              <option value="strategic-direction" selected>
                Strategic direction
              </option>
              <option value="execution">Execution &amp; transformation</option>
              <option value="fractional">Fractional leadership</option>
              <option value="advisory">Advisory</option>
              <option value="speaking">Speaking &amp; workshops</option>
              <option value="mentoring">Mentoring</option>
              <option value="other">Something else</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">Message</span>
            <textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
          </label>
          {
            TURNSTILE_SITEKEY && (
              <>
                <div
                  class="cf-turnstile"
                  data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY}
                  data-theme="light"
                />
                <script
                  is:inline
                  src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js"
                  async
                  defer
                />
              </>
            )
          }
          <button class="btn-plain" type="submit">Send it</button>
          <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
      <p class="faq-link">
        Questions first? <a href="/faq">Read the FAQ.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <script>
    const ENDPOINT = 'https://contact-form.intentionaut.workers.dev/contact';
    const form = document.getElementById('contact-form');

    form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('form-status');

      try {
        const res = await fetch(ENDPOINT, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(data),
        });
        const result = await res.json();
        if (res.ok) {
          form.reset();
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.message || "Thank you; I'll reply soon.";
        } else {
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.error || 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
        }
      } catch {
        if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
